# Chroma content pack, The Five Callings: THE COMMAND ROAD (Red, the commander), moments 1 to 9 of "The command road" in
# callings/MOMENTS-BRIEF.md: the soldier's everyday holder pair (calls WR / calls UBG, cycle s4) and the army officer's
# (calls BR / calls WUG, cycle s1); two steps, 'officer selection' (pairs D4a) and 'the army needs a new general' (pairs
# D4b); a fall and wrong, 'the report on the night that went wrong' (triads D2b); a long shot, 'the field commission'
# (triads D5a); and a crossing of the tribal world alone, 'the war leader is chosen at the gathering' (triads D6a).
# Syntax: header of chroma-library/build.py. Rules: chroma-library/SPEC.md, notes/library-spec.md and the brief's pack
# rules. Names in title:, grants:, takes_if_fails:, grants_if_fails:, requires:, holds: and aims: come from
# callings/catalogue.py, core/longshot.py and the base catalogue (chroma-library/earth_perks_titles.py); world lines
# follow the forms table of the brief (callings/worlds.py): the soldier is a hunter of the guard or a soldier of the
# realm, the army officer a leader of the hunters and the guard or a captain of the realm's army, the general the war
# leader of the clans or a warlord, general of the realm. Every moment shared by the worlds carries earth:, tribal: and
# magic: lines and an untagged scene for each of the two other worlds; an option whose act reads differently there
# carries its own wording; the works and fails lines read in every world.
# Holder pairs (moments 1 to 4): the two halves share stages, ages, holds:, rate (.5, a career) and gap (1-3); no share:
# line (the holds: gate does the drawing, as art-rungs.lib); no option takes a new title: the next rung is an aims:, and
# grants: gives only a perk plainly earned ([leading soldiers], [mentioned in dispatches], [old comrades]). Inside every
# moment each colour's mean chance is the same (a single and its cross option; a single and half of each of its two
# pairs; a single and a third of each of its three triads), so the file is even in every stage.
# Steps and the long shot carry their real chances (the brief: officer selection passed 35, a general's post 6, long
# shots 2 to 5), the same for every colour that tries for the same rung; the earned-odds lifts (helps.py, half on the
# summit) come on top in the engine. The long shot's singles carry grants_if_fails: a long shot that missed; the steps,
# at real odds, carry no perk on failure. Every option of a life event leaves one or two footprints (the footprints
# brief): a title, a counted perk or a read mark where it has one, else a foot: just before chance:.
# Content: a road of soldiers in peacetime, of training, floods, long years of command and one hard loss. Nobody is
# killed by the character and no option kills; no fighting, massacre, harm to civilians, torture or prisoner appears or
# can be picked; injuries and losses are plain and offstage (a leg broken on a night exercise, a truck that left a
# mountain road far away, a vehicle overturned on exercise); no recruit or soldier in any text is a child, and no child
# is ever in danger. The new sergeant's harm is words and punishments only. No real army, regiment, war, battle,
# country, rank title of a real country, person, place or year is named: "the army", "the academy", "the general
# staff". In the tribal world the spirits speak only through the shaman, on one optional and priced option (a closed:
# approval: line with its backfire), never by the person's own gift; modern Earth has no magic.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- soldier: calls WR / calls UBG (cycle s4)
# 1. The corporal falls on a night exercise and someone has to take charge. Each colour's single and cross option sum to
# 140 (a mean of 70): the bold carry and the lone run are the hard acts, the patient wait and the drill the steady ones.

== the corporal is hurt on exercise
tier: everyday
rate: 0.5
gap: 1-3
times: per soldier a year: about 1 in 8 sees a comrade hurt badly enough on exercise or in training to be carried off, with no officer near (estimate); training injuries are the commonest injuries in peacetime armies, most of them to the legs and feet (armed forces injury surveys); about 5 lives in 100 serve as soldiers (catalogue share)
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 17-55
calls: WR
holds: soldier
tone: trouble
life: work, friends
horizon: moment
roles: colleague, boss, friend
earth: a night exercise in the hills: the section's corporal falls on the scree and breaks a leg, and someone has to take charge and get everyone down
tribal: a night watch in the hills: the leader of the hunters' party falls among the rocks and breaks a leg, and someone has to bring everyone down to the camp
magic: a night march over the fells: the corporal of the file falls on the scree and breaks a leg, and someone has to bring everyone down to the fort
scene: Two in the morning on the exercise, high on the hill and in rain. The corporal, {colleague}, slips on the scree, goes down hard and cannot stand: the leg is broken. Seven soldiers, one radio, a map in a wet pocket and the meeting point far below, and everyone looks at everyone else, and then at {N}.
scene W: There is a drill for this, and {N} learned it in the first week: the casualty first, then the radio, then the count, then the route. Somebody has to say it out loud.
scene U: {N} pulls out the map under a torch, works out where they are to a hundred metres, and starts thinking about the gentlest way off the hill rather than the shortest.
scene B: Someone will take charge in the next minute, and whoever does will be the one the officers hear about tomorrow. {N} knows it, and so does everyone else in the section.
scene R: {N} is moving before anyone speaks: down beside the corporal, a hand on the shoulder, a joke to stop the shaking. The rain is coming sideways, and there is no time to wait for orders.
scene G: The section has eaten, slept and marched together for a year. {N} looks round at the cold faces and knows who is frightened, who is fine, and who will carry their end of a stretcher all night without a word.
scene tribal: High in the hills on the night watch, in rain, the leader of the hunters' party slips among the rocks and cannot stand: the leg is broken. Six hunters of the guard, one torch and the camp far below in the dark, and they all look at {N}.
scene magic: On the night march over the fells the corporal of the file slips on the scree and cannot stand: the leg is broken. Seven soldiers of the realm, one lantern and the fort far below, and they all look at {N}.
- W | take charge by the drill: the casualty, the radio, the count, then the route | grants: leading soldiers | aims: army officer | v: conformity, security | tribal: take charge as the old hunters taught: the hurt one, the signal fire, the count, the path | magic: take charge by the drill: the casualty, the signal horn, the count, the road | chance: 70
- U | find the gentlest way down on the map, and splint the leg before anyone moves | mark: learned a skill | v: achievement, security | tribal: find the gentlest path down by the stars, and bind the leg to a spear shaft before anyone moves | chance: 70
- B | get on the radio first, and make sure the officers know who took charge | aims: army officer | v: power, achievement | tribal: run to the ridge and light the signal fire, so the camp knows who took charge | magic: sound the horn for the fort, and make sure the captain knows who took charge | chance: 65
- R | carry the corporal down on your back, and let the others follow | grants: mentioned in dispatches | body: heavy | v: benevolence, stimulation | tribal: carry the hurt leader down the hill on your back, and let the others follow | magic: carry the corporal down on your back, and let the file follow | chance: 60
- G | keep everyone close and calm under the rocks, and wait warm for the rescue | self_control: + | v: benevolence, security | tribal: keep everyone close and calm under the overhang, and wait warm for the camp to come | magic: keep the file close and calm under the rocks, and wait warm for the fort's riders | chance: 75
- W>G | set a rota so everyone takes a turn keeping the corporal warm and talking | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: set a turn for each hunter to keep the hurt leader warm and talking | magic: set a rota so each soldier takes a turn keeping the corporal warm and talking | chance: 70
- U>W | log the time, the grid reference and every step taken, for the report | habit | v: conformity, security | tribal: mark the place with stones, and keep every step taken in mind for the elders | magic: note the hour, the place and every step taken, for the captain's report | chance: 70
- B>U | listen to how the officers run the rescue, and learn it for your own turn | door | self_control: + | v: achievement, power | tribal: watch how the old hunters bring the party in, and learn it for your own turn | magic: watch how the sergeants run the rescue, and learn it for your own turn | chance: 75
- R>B | run the whole way down alone for help, faster than anyone thinks possible | body: heavy | mark: took a wild risk | v: stimulation, achievement | tribal: run down alone through the dark to the camp, faster than anyone thinks possible | magic: run down alone through the dark to the fort, faster than anyone thinks possible | chance: 80
- G>R | sing the section's old songs all the way down, so nobody's spirit breaks | grants: old comrades | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: sing the band's old songs all the way down, so nobody's heart fails | magic: sing the company's old marching songs all the way down, so nobody's heart fails | chance: 65
works: By dawn everyone is off the hill, the broken leg is in good hands, and nobody else is hurt.
works: The story of the night goes round the next day, and {Ns} name is in it.
fails: The way down takes the whole night, two more turn their ankles, and the questions start the next morning.
fails: Help comes late, and they arrive cold, shaken and arguing over who should have done what.

# 2. A new sergeant picks on the platoon's slowest recruit, words and punishments only. The wrong is Green's means for
# Red's end (going along with the group, for the easy laugh): marked gave in to pressure and closed by approval, with
# the brief's backfire. White's complaint through the channel is closed by approval too (the platoon calls it
# informing). Singles and cross options sum to 140 for every colour.

== the platoon gets a new sergeant
tier: everyday
rate: 0.5
gap: 1-3
times: per soldier a year: about 1 in 6 serves under a sergeant or a corporal who singles one soldier out (estimate); service attitude surveys in several armies find about 1 serving soldier in 8 to 10 reporting bullying, harassment or discrimination in a year; about 5 lives in 100 serve as soldiers (catalogue share)
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 17-55
calls: UBG
holds: soldier
tone: trouble
life: work, friends
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, mentor
earth: a new sergeant comes to the platoon and picks on its slowest recruit: extra drills at dawn, a nickname, the whole platoon punished for one soldier's mistakes
tribal: a new leader of the watch picks on the slowest hunter of the guard: the worst watches, the heaviest loads, mockery at the fire
magic: a new sergeant comes to the company and rides its slowest recruit: extra drill, the latrines, names shouted across the parade ground
scene: The new sergeant has been with the platoon a fortnight and has already found a target: {colleague}, the slowest runner and the clumsiest on the range. Extra drills at dawn, a nickname that has stuck, and the whole platoon doing press-ups in the mud for every mistake {colleague} makes. Some of the others have started to join in.
scene W: The army has rules about how a sergeant may treat a soldier, and {N} has read them. Hard training is one thing; this is something else, and the rules say so.
scene U: {N} watches the sergeant for a week and sees the pattern: always {colleague}, always in front of everyone, never when an officer is near. A pattern can be written down.
scene B: The sergeant writes the reports that go up the chain, and nobody gets on by crossing them. {N} wonders what it would cost to be on the wrong side, and what it might be worth to be on the right one.
scene R: Every time the sergeant starts on {colleague}, {Ns} jaw tightens. It would feel very good to say something, loudly, right there on the parade ground.
scene G: The platoon was a family before the sergeant came: rude, awkward and close. Now it is splitting, and {colleague} eats alone. {N} feels it like weather turning.
scene tribal: The new leader of the watch has been with the guard a moon and has found a target: {colleague}, the slowest hunter, given the worst watches and the heaviest loads and mocked at the fire every night. Some of the others have started to laugh along.
scene magic: The new sergeant has been with the company a fortnight and has found a target: {colleague}, the slowest recruit, given extra drill, the latrines and a nickname shouted across the parade ground. Some of the others have started to join in.
- W | report the sergeant through the proper channel, in writing and signed | mark: helped someone in need | closed: approval: a complaint against a sergeant from the ranks; backfire: the platoon calls it informing, and the sergeant learns who wrote it | v: conformity, universalism | tribal: tell the elders at the fire, plainly, what the leader of the watch is doing | magic: report the sergeant to the captain through the proper channel, in writing and signed | chance: 60
- U | keep a dated note of every incident, until the pattern cannot be denied | self_control: + | v: security, universalism | tribal: cut a notch in a stick for every time it happens, until the pattern cannot be denied | chance: 70
- B | make yourself the sergeant's right hand, and use it to steer them off the recruit | aims: army officer | v: power, security | tribal: make yourself the watch leader's right hand, and use it to steer them off the slow hunter | chance: 65
- R | stand between the sergeant and the recruit next time, and say it out loud | mark: defied an authority | identity | v: universalism, stimulation | tribal: step between the watch leader and the slow hunter next time, and say it out loud | magic: step between the sergeant and the recruit on parade next time, and say it out loud | chance: 65
- G | sit with the recruit at meals, and bring the others back to the table | grants: old comrades | identity | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: sit with the slow hunter at the fire, and bring the others back to the circle | magic: sit with the recruit at mess, and bring the others back to the table | chance: 70
- W>G | set up evening runs for the whole section, so the recruit is never last alone | grants: leading soldiers | habit | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: set up runs at dusk for the whole guard, so the slow hunter is never last alone | magic: set up evening runs for the whole file, so the recruit is never last alone | chance: 80
- U>W | look up the regulations, and show the platoon commander which ones are broken | identity | v: conformity, universalism | tribal: remind the elders of the old rule that the guard shames nobody at the fire | magic: look up the articles of the realm's army, and show the captain which are broken | chance: 70
- B>U | buy the old quartermaster a drink, and learn what moves the new sergeant | v: achievement, power | tribal: bring the oldest hunter a share of meat, and learn what moves the new watch leader | magic: buy the old quartermaster a cup, and learn what moves the new sergeant | chance: 75
- R>B | get the platoon to stand together next time, so the sergeant faces all of them | binds | v: stimulation, power | tribal: get the whole guard to stand together next time, so the watch leader faces all of them | magic: get the company to stand together next time, so the sergeant faces all of them | chance: 75
- G>R | look away, and laugh along with the others, so you stay one of the platoon | mark: gave in to pressure | closed: approval: laughing along while a recruit is picked on; backfire: the recruit leaves the army, and the inquiry asks who saw it and said nothing | self_control: - | v: hedonism, conformity | tribal: look away, and laugh along at the fire, so you stay one of the guard | magic: look away, and laugh along on parade, so you stay one of the company | chance: 70
works: Within a month things change the way {N} meant them to, and nobody eats alone any more.
works: The pressure eases, and at the next test the slowest of them finishes with the others cheering.
fails: Nothing changes, and before long {colleague} asks to be sent somewhere else.
fails: Word of it gets back, and the next month is a long one for {N}.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- army officer: calls BR / calls WUG (cycle s1)
# 3. An order from above would put the officer's own soldiers at needless risk to meet a timetable (a pass in fog and
# ice, a river in spate). The brief's five answers: obey (White), refuse (Red, marked defied an authority and closed by
# approval), a smarter plan (Blue), the order asked for in writing (Black), over the commander's head (Black's means for
# Red's end). No option touches anyone outside the unit. Singles and cross options sum to 140 for every colour.

== an order you think is wrong
tier: everyday
rate: 0.5
gap: 1-3
times: per army officer a year: about 1 in 5 is given an order they believe puts their soldiers at needless risk, most often to keep to a timetable (estimate); about 6 lives in 1,000 are army officers (catalogue share)
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 20-62
calls: BR
holds: army officer
tone: trouble
life: work
horizon: moment
roles: boss, colleague, mentor
earth: an order from the commanding officer: drive the company's trucks over the mountain pass tonight, in fog and ice, so the exercise can start on time at dawn
tribal: the elder of the guard orders the hunters across the swollen river tonight, in the dark, so they reach the far hills before the herd moves
magic: an order from the commander of the fort: take the company's wagons over the high pass tonight, in fog and ice, so the review can begin at dawn
scene: The order comes down at six in the evening from {boss}, the commanding officer: the company's trucks are to cross the pass tonight, so the exercise can start on time at dawn. The forecast says fog and black ice, the drivers have been awake since five, and the old road has no barrier on the drop side. {N} reads it twice.
scene W: An order is an order, and an army runs because people carry them out. But the rules also say an officer answers for the soldiers' safety, and tonight the two pull different ways.
scene U: There must be a better plan than this one: a later start, a lower road, a convoy at first light with the gritter in front. {N} pulls out the map and the timetable.
scene B: {boss} writes {Ns} reports. Obeying costs nothing tonight, and refusing could cost a career; but if a truck goes over the edge, the name on the movement order will be {Ns}.
scene R: {N} thinks of the drivers, red-eyed in the canteen, and feels the anger rise. Nobody who has driven that road at night in ice would give this order.
scene G: {N} knows every driver by name, and the families of half of them. The exercise will happen with or without tonight; each of the drivers has one life.
scene tribal: At dusk the elder of the guard sends word: the hunters are to cross the swollen river tonight, in the dark, to reach the far hills before the herd moves. The water is high and brown, the hunters have walked since dawn, and {N} leads them.
scene magic: At dusk a rider brings the order from {boss}, the commander of the fort: the company's wagons are to cross the high pass tonight, in fog and ice, so the review can begin at dawn. The drivers are spent, the road has no wall on the drop side, and {N} leads them.
- W | carry out the order to the letter, with every safety check done twice | v: conformity, security | tribal: take the hunters over as the elder ordered, every rope and handhold checked twice | magic: carry out the order to the letter, every wagon and wheel checked twice | chance: 60
- U | work out a later, safer plan that still meets the start, and send it up | aims: general | v: achievement, security | tribal: find a safer crossing upstream that still reaches the far hills in time, and send word | magic: work out a later, safer road that still meets the dawn, and send it to the fort | chance: 70
- B | ask for the order in writing and signed, so the risk sits with whoever gave it | v: power, security | tribal: ask the elder to give the order again before all the hunters, so the risk sits with whoever gave it | magic: ask for the order under the commander's seal, so the risk sits with whoever gave it | chance: 80
- R | refuse to send the drivers tonight, and tell the commander why, face to face | mark: defied an authority | closed: approval: an order refused; backfire: a formal warning on the record, and the commanding officer does not forget it | v: benevolence, self-direction | tribal: refuse to take the hunters into the river tonight, and tell the elder why, face to face | magic: refuse to send the wagons tonight, and tell the commander why, face to face | chance: 65
- G | let the drivers sleep six hours, cross at first light, and take what comes | identity | v: benevolence, security | tribal: let the hunters sleep, cross at first light when the water drops, and take what comes | magic: let the drivers sleep six hours, cross at first light, and take what comes | chance: 65
- W>U | ring the weather office and the road police, and get the facts on paper first | v: conformity, security | tribal: send the best tracker to read the river and the sky, and bring back the facts first | magic: send riders to the pass and the weather-wise, and get the facts set down first | chance: 80
- U>B | show the commander a plan that makes the delay look like their own idea | v: power, achievement | tribal: show the elder a way that makes waiting look like the elder's own idea | magic: show the commander a plan that makes the delay look like the commander's own idea | chance: 70
- B>R | go above the commander's head to the general staff, and get the order stopped | mark: made an enemy | v: power, benevolence | tribal: go over the elder's head to the leader of all the guard, and get the order stopped | magic: send a rider over the commander's head to the general's tent, and get the order stopped | chance: 60
- R>G | drive the pass alone first in the light truck, to see the road for the others | body: light | mark: took a wild risk | v: benevolence, stimulation | tribal: wade the river alone first on a rope, to find the footing for the others | magic: ride the pass alone first, to see the road for the others | chance: 75
- G>W | gather the drivers, and agree a rule together: nobody drives who has not slept | grants: leading soldiers | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: gather the hunters, and agree together that nobody crosses who has not slept | magic: gather the drivers, and agree together that nobody drives who has not slept | chance: 75
works: The night passes without harm, and in the morning nobody has to explain anything they cannot.
works: The commanders above hear how it was handled, and remember the name.
fails: It goes wrong from the first hour, and {N} spends the week answering for it.
fails: The order stands, the night is long and frightening, and {boss} is cool with {N} for months.

# 4. A soldier of the unit did not come home from a deployment far away: a truck that left a mountain road at night,
# told plainly and offstage, with nobody to blame in the text. The brief's four answers (visit the family, speak at the
# memorial, push the inquiry, keep the unit together) are White's, Red's, Blue's and Green's singles; Black's briefs the
# general staff first. Singles and cross options sum to 140 for every colour.

== the unit comes home one short
tier: everyday
rate: 0.5
gap: 1-3
times: per army officer a year: about 1 in 25 loses a soldier of their own unit to an accident, an illness or an operation abroad (estimate); in peacetime, road and training accidents are among the commonest causes of death in armies (armed forces mortality reports); about 6 lives in 1,000 are army officers (catalogue share)
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 20-62
calls: WUG
holds: army officer
tone: trouble
life: work, friends, meaning
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, mentor, friend
earth: the unit is home from a deployment far away, one soldier short: a truck left a mountain road in the last week, and a family is waiting for answers
tribal: the guard is back from the long journey to the far hills, one hunter short: the river took one of them at a crossing, and a hearth is waiting for someone to come and speak
magic: the company is back from the long garrison in the north, one soldier short: a supply wagon went off a mountain road, and a family in the town is waiting for word
scene: The unit came home on Tuesday to the families on the parade ground, one short. In the last week of the deployment a truck left a mountain road at night, and one of the drivers did not come home; the funeral was last week. Now the unit is on leave, the inquiry has begun, and the driver's family has asked to see the officer who led them.
scene W: {N} signed the movement orders for that convoy. There is a duty to the family, a duty to the inquiry and a duty to the unit, and {N} means to keep all three.
scene U: The report says the truck left the road in darkness. {N} wants to know why: the road, the truck, the hours the driver had worked, and the order that put them out there at night.
scene B: Inquiries look for someone to blame, and {N} knows how these things go: the name on the order is usually the one that stays. {N} also knows who in the chain could make it go another way.
scene R: {N} keeps seeing the driver's grin at the last roll call, and cannot sit still with it. The grief comes out as anger: at the road, at the army, at {N}.
scene G: The unit is scattered on leave, each of them carrying it home alone. {N} thinks of the driver's mother, of the soldiers who shared that truck, and of how a unit either holds together after a loss or comes apart.
scene tribal: The guard came back from the far hills one short: at a river crossing the water took one of the hunters, and the others could not reach him. The band has mourned, and now the hunter's mother has asked to see the one who led them.
scene magic: The company came back from the long garrison in the north one short: a supply wagon went off a mountain road at night, and its driver did not come home. The town has buried the driver, and the family has asked to see the captain who led them.
- W | visit the family, answer every question honestly, and keep in touch | mark: kept your word | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: go to the hunter's hearth, answer every question honestly, and come back every moon | magic: ride to the family's house, answer every question honestly, and keep writing | chance: 75
- U | push the inquiry for the true cause: the road, the truck, the hours worked | v: universalism, achievement | tribal: walk the crossing again, and find out truly why the water took the hunter | magic: press the inquiry for the true cause: the road, the wagon, the hours driven | chance: 60
- B | brief the general staff before the inquiry does, and shape what they hear first | aims: general | v: power, security | tribal: speak to the leader of all the guard before the elders meet, and shape what they hear first | magic: ride to the general's staff before the inquiry sits, and shape what they hear first | chance: 70
- R | speak at the memorial from the heart, without notes | v: benevolence, stimulation | tribal: speak at the mourning fire from the heart | magic: speak at the burying from the heart, without notes | chance: 70
- G | ring every soldier on leave, and bring the unit back together at one table | grants: old comrades | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: go to every hunter's hearth, and bring the guard back together at one fire | magic: visit every soldier on leave, and bring the company back together at one table | chance: 65
- W>U | give the inquiry every order, log and timing, including your own mistakes | mark: owned up | identity | v: universalism, conformity | tribal: tell the elders every word and step of the crossing, your own mistakes too | magic: give the inquiry every order, log and hour, your own mistakes too | chance: 65
- U>B | work out what the inquiry will ask, and have every answer ready | v: security, achievement | tribal: work out what the elders will ask, and have every answer ready | chance: 80
- B>R | call in favours to fund a race every year in the driver's name | v: benevolence, power | tribal: call in what the bands owe, for a feast every year in the hunter's name | magic: call in favours for a tournament every year in the driver's name | chance: 70
- R>G | take the soldiers who shared the truck away to the hills, and let them talk | v: benevolence, stimulation | tribal: take the hunters who were at the crossing up into the hills, and let them talk | magic: take the soldiers who rode with the wagon away to the hills, and let them talk | chance: 70
- G>W | keep the old custom: an empty place at the unit's table, every year | habit | v: tradition, benevolence | tribal: keep the old custom: an empty place at the guard's fire, every year | magic: keep the old custom: an empty place at the company's table, every year | chance: 75
works: They hold together, and the family knows the one they lost is not forgotten.
works: A year on, the answers are clear, and the loss has changed something for the better.
fails: They scatter, and nobody quite talks about it again.
fails: The family's grief turns to anger, and much of it falls on {N}.

# ================================================================ steps

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. officer selection (pairs D4a)
# The academy's selection board: every colour's way through it passes at the real chance, 35, and makes an [army
# officer] with [an officer's commission] (the rule in roles.py grants it too). It comes to a soldier of two years, a
# graduate or one who has done national service (LIFE_CALLINGS), so every act is written to fit all three. The pairs at
# 75 are the honest other ways: the slow road through the ranks, the practice papers first, the mountain leader course
# first, an old officer of the town to sponsor it, or turning it down for now. Every colour's mean is 55.

== officer selection
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult
age: 20-40
holds: soldier | graduate | national service done
per_year: 0 0 .08 .04 0 0
drivers: era+.1
times: per soldier of two years, graduate or one who has done national service, aged 20 to 40, a year: about 1 in 12 in the twenties and fewer later goes before an officer selection board (estimate); about 1 member in 6 of an active army is an officer (US Department of Defense figures in the catalogue), and selection boards pass about 1 candidate in 3 (estimate); about 6 lives in 1,000 become army officers (catalogue share)
likelier: a sergeant who pushes, a degree and a fit body, years when the army is growing and short of young officers
rarer: a record with the police, poor health, a family that wants a safer life, a year of cuts to the army
gap: 1-3
domain: career.5
rite: young_adult
tone: mixed
life: work, school
horizon: months
roles: mentor, boss, parent, colleague, rival
earth: the officer selection board: three days of tests, interviews and a muddy field, and a place at the academy for about one candidate in three
tribal: the elders of the guard test who may lead the hunters: three days of tracking, carrying, a river crossing and speaking at the fire
magic: the realm's captains hold their selection at the old fort: three days of trials, questions and a muddy field, for a place at the officers' school
scene: The letter says three days at the selection board: written tests, an interview before a panel of senior officers, a talk to give, and a field of mud with a plank, two oil drums and a team of strangers who must all be got across. About one candidate in three is offered a place at the academy. {mentor} has said for years that {N} should go.
scene W: {N} has read the board's handbook until the pages are soft: the qualities it looks for, the dress for each day, the order of the tests. To lead soldiers is a duty before it is a rank.
scene U: The command tasks are puzzles with planks and drums and a clock running. {N} has been practising them on the kitchen table with matchsticks and a ruler.
scene B: The board is the first gate on a long road, and {N} has looked up where the officers of other years ended up: some of them sit on the general staff now.
scene R: {N} just wants to get into the mud and lead. The written tests feel like a fence to climb on the way to the real thing.
scene G: Nobody in {Ns} family has been an officer. {parent} says the old soldiers of the town will be proud, and {N} wonders what it means to rise above the people {N} came up with.
scene tribal: The elders of the guard will choose new leaders of the hunters this season. For three days the young hunters track, carry, take a party across the river and speak at the fire, and the elders watch every one of them.
scene magic: The realm's captains hold their selection at the old fort every spring: three days of trials, questions before a panel of captains, and a field of mud where a team of strangers must be got over a ditch with two barrels and a plank. A captain's commission waits for perhaps one in three.
