fails: The last day goes badly, a task falls apart in front of the panel, and the journey home is very long.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 6. the army needs a new general (pairs D4b)
# The summit, a facet on the officer of twelve years: every colour's bid for the post at its real chance, 6 (the brief:
# a general's post; helps.py lifts it by half the earned odds). Black's lobbying over the army's head is closed by
# approval with its backfire. The pairs at 74 are the honest other ways: the officers' academy to command instead, a
# rival backed for the post one really wants, a young officer taken on to teach, a better officer served, the far posting
# nobody wants. Every colour's mean is 40.

== the army needs a new general
tier: life event
stages: adult mature
age: 40-62
holds: army officer
tenure: 12-100
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .04 0
drivers: era+.2 fortune+.2
times: per army officer of twelve years or more a year: about 1 in 30 is in the running when a general's post falls free (estimate); armies have under 1 general for every 1,000 soldiers on active duty (US Department of Defense figures in the catalogue), and most officers leave the army long before; about 3 lives in 100,000 become generals (catalogue share)
likelier: a command that went well, a mention in dispatches or an award, years when the army is changing and needs new leaders, a patron on the general staff
rarer: a quarrel with the government, an inquiry on the record, a shrinking army with fewer posts, a career spent far from the capital
gap: 3-8
domain: career.5
tone: mixed
life: work, publiclife
horizon: months
roles: boss, rival, mentor, colleague, partner
earth: a general retires, and the selection panel of the general staff will choose a successor from a short list of senior officers
tribal: the old war leader of the clans can no longer walk the hills, and asks the leaders of the guard which of them will carry the spear after
magic: a general of the realm has retired to the country, and the council of war will name a new one from among the realm's captains
scene: A general is retiring in the spring, and the selection panel of the general staff will choose a successor from a short list. {Ns} name is on it after twenty years of postings, and so is {rival}'s, an officer with a famous family and friends in the government. One post, perhaps six names, and a panel that meets behind closed doors.
scene W: {N} has served twenty years by the rules: every report clean, every order carried out or lawfully questioned. If that is not enough for the panel, then the rules mean less than {N} thought.
scene U: For years {N} has been writing, privately, about what the army will need in twenty years' time. The panel will ask, and for once the answer is ready.
scene B: Six names and one post. {N} knows which members of the panel owe {rival} favours, which ones dine with ministers, and which ones have not yet made up their minds.
scene R: {N} has led from the front for twenty years, and the soldiers know it. The panel can read the record; {N} would rather stand in front of them and say what the army needs.
scene G: {N} has watched two generations of soldiers come up through the ranks, and some of them lead units of their own now. If the post comes, it comes; the army will need its old hands whoever is chosen.
scene tribal: The old war leader of the clans can no longer walk the hills, and at the autumn gathering will hand the spear to one of the leaders of the guard. {N} has led the hunters for many winters, and so has {rival}, whose father carried the spear before.
scene magic: A general of the realm has retired to the country, and the council of war will name a new one before the spring muster. {Ns} name is among the captains spoken of, and so is {rival}'s, a captain of a great house with friends at court.
