# ================================================================ fall and wrong

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7. the report on the night that went wrong (triads D2b)
# A friend, tired and driving too fast on exercise, turned a truck over, and a soldier was hurt (a broken arm, mending
# now). The wrong is Blue's single, deception by wit for a friend's sake: the cause written as a fault in the old truck,
# marked hid a wrong, closed by law with the brief's backfire, and a failed try takes [rank] (takes_if_fails, as the
# Art pack's forgery). The others: the report written true (White), true and showing who got the hurt soldier out
# (Black), the friend urged to own up first (Red), the hurt soldier visited every week (Green), and the triads: the
# drill rewritten, a share of the blame taken, retraining asked for, the friend taken to the doctor, the hurt soldier
# asked first. Chances are set by act and solved so every colour's mean is 71.

== the report on the night that went wrong
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 18-65
holds: army officer | soldier | general
per_year: 0 0 .01 .015 .01 0
drivers: harsh+.2
times: per soldier, officer or general a year: about 1 in 80 has to write or sign a report on an accident in which a friend's mistake hurt someone (estimate); armies look into thousands of training and vehicle accidents a year, and incomplete or shaded accident reports are a common finding of the inquiries that follow (estimate); about 5 lives in 100 serve as soldiers (catalogue share)
likelier: a tired unit at the end of a long exercise, old vehicles, a friend at the wheel, a unit where mistakes are punished hard
rarer: a unit with good drills and rested drivers, a name known for writing it straight
gap: 5-15
domain: career.5
tone: trouble
life: work, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, colleague, boss, mentor
earth: on an exercise a friend's mistake turned a truck over, a soldier was hurt, and the report is due on Friday with a signature on it
tribal: on the long hunt a friend's hurry overturned the raft at a crossing, a hunter of the guard was hurt, and the elders want to hear how it happened
magic: on manoeuvres a friend's mistake turned a supply wagon over, a soldier was hurt, and the captain wants the report by the end of the week
scene: On the last night of the exercise {friend}, tired and driving too fast on a forest track, turned a truck onto its side. A soldier in the back was hurt: a broken arm and a night in hospital, mending now. Nobody else saw the speed but {N}, and the report is due on Friday with {Ns} signature on it. {friend} has asked, quietly, for the road to be blamed.
scene W: A report is a promise that what it says is true. {N} has signed hundreds, and never one with a word in it that was not so.
scene U: {N} has been over it a dozen times: the speed, the bend, the hours {friend} had been driving, the drill that let a tired driver take the wheel. The truth is more interesting than the blame.
scene B: An inquiry will read the report, and an inquiry wants a name. {N} weighs whose name it will be, what each version costs, and who will owe what afterwards.
scene R: {friend} has been {Ns} friend since the first week of training. Putting that name in a report feels like a betrayal, and so does lying for it.
scene G: The hurt soldier is mending, {friend} is sick with guilt, and the unit is holding its breath. {N} thinks about what the unit needs to come through this whole.
scene tribal: On the long hunt {friend}, tired and in a hurry, overturned the raft at the crossing, and a hunter of the guard was hurt: a broken arm, mending now. Nobody else saw how it happened but {N}, and the elders want to hear it at the fire. {friend} has asked, quietly, for the river to be blamed.
scene magic: On the last night of manoeuvres {friend}, tired and driving the team too hard on a forest road, turned a supply wagon over. A soldier riding on it was hurt: a broken arm, mending now. Nobody else saw but {N}, and the captain wants the report by the end of the week. {friend} has asked, quietly, for the road to be blamed.
