# ================================================================ world-only

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. the war leader is chosen at the gathering (only: tribal; triads D6a)
# The tribal crossing: the clans gather to choose who will lead them if raiders come. No fighting is in the moment. It
# comes to a leader of the hunters and the guard of six winters or a hunter of the guard of twelve (LIFE_CALLINGS), and
# the brief gives each a different rung: the war leader of the clans ([general]) at 6 for the leader, a leader of the
# hunters and the guard ([army officer]) at 35 for the hunter. A career holds one title at a time, so the two never meet
# in one person, and each rung's tries carry `requires: <the rung below> | without: impossible`, so nobody is offered a
# rung that does not fit: the five singles are the leader's bids for the spear, and a full cross cycle (s2) holds the
# hunter's bids for the guard. The five triads are open to both: another band's leader put forward, a seat at the
# council fire, the choice left to the spirits (the shaman's price, a closed: approval line with its backfire: the
# spirits speak through someone else, never through the person's gift), no war leader while no raiders come, the stores
# and signal fires kept. So each holder meets ten options, even on their own (singles or cycle, and the triads), and the
# moment is even in every colour: 6, 35 and 70 give every colour 37. A life event with a cross cycle beside its
# combinations is rare (the Library's 'a baby on the way, planned or not'); build.py accepts the layout.

== the war leader is chosen at the gathering
tier: life event
only: tribal
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-80
holds: army officer | soldier
tenure: 3-99
per_year: 0 0 0 .02 .02 .01
times: per leader of the hunters and the guard of six winters, or hunter of the guard of twelve, in the tribal world, a year: about 1 in 50 is at a gathering where the clans choose a war leader against raiders (estimate); bands of hunters and gatherers chose a war leader only when a threat was near, for a season, and most of the time had none (ethnographies of band societies; estimate)
likelier: word of raiders in the far valleys, a hard winter that brings strangers near, an old war leader gone
rarer: long years of peace between the clans, a gathering that breaks up in a quarrel
gap: 5-12
domain: career.5
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: months
roles: elder, rival, mentor, friend
tribal: the clans gather at the autumn camp to choose who will lead them if raiders come, and the elders of every band will speak
scene tribal: The clans have gathered at the autumn camp by the great river, and word has come of strangers raiding in the far valleys. Before the bands go to their winter places the elders will choose who leads them all if the raiders come this way: a war leader for the winter, and leaders for the guard of each band. {N} has walked with the guard for many winters, and the elders' eyes keep coming back to {N}.
scene tribal W: There is an old law for the choosing: the elders speak in turn, the oath is sworn at the fire, and the one chosen answers to all the clans. {N} means to keep it.
scene tribal U: {N} has walked every pass into the valley and knows where the clans could watch for strangers and where the signal fires would carry. A war leader should know such things before anything else.
scene tribal B: The biggest clans will decide it, whatever the elders say. {N} knows which chiefs listen to whom, and what each of them wants from the winter.
scene tribal R: The whole camp is restless with the news, and {N} feels it too: the wish to stand up and be the one who leads, now, before the moment goes.
scene tribal G: The clans have met at this bend of the river since before anyone's grandmother's grandmother. Raiders have come and gone, and the river and the clans are still here. Whoever leads, {N} thinks, should remember that.
- W | stand before the clans by the old law, and swear the war leader's oath | title: general | requires: army officer | without: impossible | identity | v: conformity, tradition | chance: 6
- U | show the gathering how the clans would hold the passes if raiders came | title: general | requires: army officer | without: impossible | v: achievement, security | chance: 6
- B | win the chiefs of the biggest clans to your side before the gathering opens | title: general | requires: army officer | without: impossible | aims: general | v: power, achievement | chance: 6
- R | stand up at the fire, and say plainly that you will lead them, and why | title: general | requires: army officer | without: impossible | mark: took a wild risk | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 6
- G | let the hunters of your guard speak your name at the fire, and wait | title: general | requires: army officer | without: impossible | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 6
