works: The clans choose, the winter passes without raiders, and {N} walks the camp with a new place in it.
works: Whatever {N} chose, the gathering ends at peace, and the bands go to their winter places trusting the choice.
fails: The elders choose {rival}, and {N} carries {rival}'s word to the far camps all winter.
fails: The gathering breaks up in a quarrel, and every band goes home with its own plan.
